# OKO: declarative list of paths removed from the packed firmware image.
#
# Every non-empty line is a path relative to either
#   output/out/rootfs_uclibc_rv1106/  (rootfs)
#   output/out/oem/                   (oem)
# The same list is applied to both directories, so a path that exists only in
# one of them is normal.  Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
# Shell globs are allowed; a missing path is reported as a warning, not an
# error, so an incremental build or another board config still packs.
#
# project/build.sh:__RUN_POST_CLEAN_FILES applies the list, and
# tools/native/check_image_contents.sh uses it as the forbidden set.
#
# Keep this file in sync with the "Что удаляется" section of the plan:
# .kilo/plans/1794228198214-slim-image-unused-removal-plan.md

# Safe, self-contained vendor test binaries (no OKO service references them).
usr/bin/modetest
usr/bin/dumpsys